--- !u!114 &2084892190
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2084892187}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 72dcd122254073845a271b4898476ffc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MuseumTerminalDisplay
  pages:
  - title: I. THE FIRST SHORES
    eraCode: APOLLO 11 // TRANQUILITY BASE // 1969 A.D.
    bodyText: 'For four billion years, Earth life was bound to its planetary cradle.

      In July 1969, two Terrans stepped onto the regolith of the Moon.

      Left upon the ladder of the descent stage was a stainless steel plaque:

      "Here men from the planet Earth first set foot upon the Moon. We came in peace for all mankind."'
  - title: II. THE MESSAGE IN A BOTTLE
    eraCode: VOYAGER 1 & 2 // THE HELIOPAUSE // 1977 A.D.
    bodyText: 'Carried aboard twin nuclear-powered probes cast toward the stars,

      the Golden Record contains 115 encoded images, greetings in 55 languages,

      and a 90-minute sonic journey: rainstorms, birdsong, Bach, and human brainwaves.

      Constructed of gold-plated copper, it will endure intact for over a billion years.'
  - title: III. THE INTERSTELLAR EMBASSY
    eraCode: THE KARDASHEV THRESHOLD // DEEP TIME
    bodyText: 'Long after Earth''s oceans boil and the Sun swells into a red giant,

      the Voyager records will silently cruise the Orion Arm between the stars.

      Even if Terran civilization ceases to exist, this gold disc testifies forever:

      We lived, we loved, and we reached outward to find you.'
  currentPageIndex: 0
  titleTextMesh: {fileID: 749630119}
  bodyTextMesh: {fileID: 233106701}
  footerTextMesh: {fileID: 526370156}
  terminalScreenLight: {fileID: 1671852954}
  audioSource: {fileID: 2084892189}
  switchPageClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f9a879c27c464e6439a51ed5d6159d7a, type: 3}
